bwBlockList [SimTalk] - lane A or B
Returns the blocking list in the backward direction of the specified lane of the TwoLaneTrack designated by
<Path>.
Remarks
Specify the optional parameter of data type table, to make bwBlockList write the objects contained in the
Backward Blocking List into this list.
Do not specify the parameter, to make bwBlockList return an array containing the objects contained in the
Backward Blocking List. The array is one-dimensional and only contains the objects in the blocking list. If
you need the start times of the blockages, which are contained in the blocking table, you can query them
from the object with the attribute BlockingStartTime.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.A.bwBlockList([BackwardBlockingList:table]) → any
<Path>.B.bwBlockList([BackwardBlockingList:table]) → any
Parameter
The optional parameter BackwardBlockingList of data type table designates the name of the table, which
can be a DataTable or a local variable, into which the method writes the values.
Plant Simulation automatically generates the format of this table with two columns.
Column 1 has the data type object and contains all Transporters that unsuccessfully tried to move to the
object.
Column 2 contains the simulation time at which the Transporters attempted to enter the object. The
number of rows matches the number of Transporters in the blocking list.
Return Value
The return value has the data type any.
Is an array containing all MUs in the Backward Blocking List of the TwoLaneTrack on the specified lane if
you do not specify the optional parameter.
bwBlockList [SimTalk] - lane A or B
11-2504 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Example
MyTwoLaneTrack.B.bwBlocklist(DataTable)
SimTalk
BlockingStarttime [SimTalk]
BwBlockListEntry1 [SimTalk]
See also
Backward Blocking List
Check the Contents List of the Stations
