getRouteLength [SimTalk] - lane A or B
Returns the shortest route from the lane of the TwoLaneTrack designated by <Path> to the target and
returns the length of this route.
Remarks
The destination can either be a material flow object, which can be reached directly via Connectors, or a
destination, which you typed into a sensor.
Note
As the route is intended for Transporters, Plant Simulation only takes objects of type Track and
TwoLaneTrack into consideration, when computing the route.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.A.getRouteLength(Target:path[, Backwards:boolean, Position:length, 
ObjectsAlongRoute:table, RouteWeightingAttribute:string] → length
<Path>.B.getRouteLength(Target:path[, Backwards:boolean, Position:length, 
ObjectsAlongRoute:table, RouteWeightingAttribute:string] → length
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Target of data type object designates the target.
• The optional parameter Backwards of data type boolean designates the direction in which Plant
Simulation looks for a route. True stands for backward, false stands for forward, which is the default
setting.
• The optional parameter Position of data type length designates the position on the lane at which the
search starts. If you do not specify the parameter, Plant Simulation starts searching at the end of
the lane if you search forward, or it starts searching at the beginning if you search backward. This is
particularly important if the Destination is a sensor, which is located on the lane of the TwoLaneTrack
itself.
• The optional parameter ObjectsAlongRoute of data type table writes the objects along the route into the
specified table.
• The optional parameter RouteWeightingAttribute of data type string sets the name of the attribute for
the route weighting attribute for automatic routing. If the parameter is not passed, Plant Simulation
does not weight the lengths of the routes.
getRouteLength [SimTalk] - lane A or B
11-2512 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Return Value
The return value has the data type length.
Is -1 if Plant Simulation did not find a route.
Example
print TwoLaneTrack5.B.getRouteLength(Track26)
SimTalk
Destination [SimTalk] - sensors
RouteWeightingAttr [SimTalk] - Transporter
getRouteLength [SimTalk] - lane A or B
Plant Simulation Help 11-2513
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

pred [SimTalk] - lane A or B
Returns the direct predecessor of the designated lane of the TwoLaneTrack designated by <Path>.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.A.pred([PredecessorNumber:integer:=1]) → object
<Path>.B.pred([PredecessorNumber:integer:=1]) → object
Parameter
The optional parameter PredecessorNumber of data type integer designates the n-th predecessor of the
specified lane of the TwoLaneTrack. The objects have to be connected for this to work.
Default Value of the Parameter
The default value is 1.
Return Value
The return value has the data type object.
Example
if MyTwoLaneTrack.A.pred(3) = TwoLaneTrack1 
  ...
end
See also
succ [SimTalk] - lane A or B
pred [SimTalk] - lane A or B
