predConnector [SimTalk] - lane A or B
Returns the incoming Connector connected directly with the specified lane of the TwoLaneTrack
designated by <Path>. Adding and deleting connections may change the index number of a connection.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.A.predConnector([PredecessorNumber:integer:=1]) → object
<Path>.B.predConnector([PredecessorNumber:integer:=1]) → object
Parameter
The optional parameter PredecessorNumber of data type integer designates the n-th preceding Connector
of the specified lane of the TwoLaneTrack.
Default Value of the Parameter
The default value is 1.
Return Value
The return value has the data type object.
VOID if the connection does not exist.
Example
for var i := MyTwoLaneTrack.B.NumPred downto 1 // deletes connections
   MyTwoLaneTrack.B.predConnector(i).deleteObject
next
SimTalk
