succ [SimTalk] - lane A or B
Returns the direct successor of the specified lane of the TwoLaneTrack designated by <Path>.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.A.succ([SuccessorNumber:integer:=1]) → object
<Path>.B.succ([SuccessorNumber:integer:=1]) → object
Parameter
The optional parameter SuccessorNumber of data type integer designates the number of the successor on
the specified lane of the TwoLaneTrack. The objects have to be connected for this to work.
Default Value of the Parameter
The default value is 1, meaning the first successor on the lane.
Return Value
The return value has the data type object.
Note
If the n-th successor of the object is an Interface, Plant Simulation does not return the Interface itself,
but the successor of the Interface. If this again is an Interface, it will be tracked until Plant Simulation
reaches a material flow object which can accept MUs.
If the n-th successor of the object is a Frame, Plant Simulation does not return the Frame itself, but the
successor of the Interface inserted into this Frame.
If an Interface only has a single successor, this successor is uniquely identified and will be used,
independent of the exit strategy of the Interface.
If an Interface has several successors, the successor is identified according to its exit strategy. If you
selected a blocking exit strategy, the strategy determines the successor no matter if it can accept a MU at
the moment or not.
If you selected a non-blocking exit strategy, Plant Simulation searches for the next successor that can
accept a MU according to the selected exit strategy.
succ [SimTalk] - lane A or B
11-2518 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

If none of the successors can accept a MU, the method returns VOID. The successor that can accept a MU
next cannot be determined at that point in time. This does not apply if there is only a single successor.
Example
if MyTwoLaneTrack.B.succ = TwoLaneTrack1
  ...
end
SimTalk
pred [SimTalk] - lane A or B
succ [SimTalk] - lane A or B
